WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.730
MARKUS KLUTE: Hello, and
welcome back to 8.701.

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:10.910
In this class, we'll
talk about spin.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.270
If you remember the discussion
on relativistic kinematics

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:19.910
we had last week,
you noticed that I

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:26.090
discussed the decay of a
pion, say a neutral pion,

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:28.940
into an electron and--

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:32.659
a positron and an electron.

00:00:32.659 --> 00:00:35.270
And we were able to calculate
the velocity of those two

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:37.460
particles, the electron
and the positron,

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:40.790
quite easily by knowing the
mass of the pion and the masses

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:42.600
of the electron
and the positron,

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.040
which is served into the
rest frame of the pion,

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.780
and we can calculate
our velocity.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.830
I also told you that this
decay is highly suppressed

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:54.210
because of the spins of
the particles involved.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:58.280
The pion has spin zero, and
the electron and the positron

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:01.400
have spin 1/2, but
it is not easily

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.430
possible to align the
electron and the positron

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:08.720
such that the spins align to 0.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.246
So therefore, this decay
is not usually possible.

00:01:12.246 --> 00:01:16.340
Now, let's dive a
little bit into this.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:21.500
In quantum mechanics, the spin
of a particle with a vector

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.130
is quantized, and in terms of
its length and its components.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:27.680
You calculate the length
of the spin vector [? S. ?]

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.350
You find that it's
square root of f

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:34.170
times s plus 1 in
units of h-bar.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:37.110
The components, and along
any axis, actually--

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.330
and in this case
here, the d-axis--

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:44.530
have eigenvalues, and
they are listed here.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:49.040
And we find that there is
2s plus 1 possible values.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.130
So I'll pick here, just
arbitrarily, the z axis.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:55.550
But the question-- it's
an obvious question--

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:58.885
which axis is a sensible
choice for this problem?

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:04.570
So I want you to actually stop
here and think about this.

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:06.250
What are sensible options?

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:12.280
If you want to get an eigenvalue
with the physical state

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:16.480
of particles, which axis are
the right ones to choose--

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.130
or, sensible?

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:20.950
There's no right and
wrong in this discussion.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:23.386
Let me motivate this.

00:02:23.386 --> 00:02:26.050
If you look at the orbital
momentum of a particle,

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:30.130
that's given by r cross
p, where p is the momentum

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:32.180
vector of the particle.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:35.230
So now, if you're looking
at the total momentum,

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:38.170
we have to look add
the angular momentum

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.790
and the spin of the
particle together.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:44.430
So as shown in
this picture here,

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:47.880
you see that the
parallel component--

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:51.150
the component in parallel
to the slide direction--

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:55.050
is 0 by definition, because
the cross-product is defined--

00:02:57.407 --> 00:02:59.490
the angular momentum is
defined as a cross-product

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.260
with the momentum.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:06.810
So this is a nice choice of
coordinate system or of axis--

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:10.600
namely, that is the choice of
the momentum of the particle.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:13.710
So you find that the total
momentum perpendicular

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.920
is the spin of the
particle perpendicular,

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:21.688
and the transverse component
is its angular momentum,

00:03:21.688 --> 00:03:24.105
the orbital angular momentum,
and the spin of the particle

00:03:24.105 --> 00:03:27.280
in the transverse direction.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:30.340
This, then, immediately
gets us to a new definition,

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:31.940
then of helicity.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.570
You can define the
helicity of a particle

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:37.750
as the spin of the
particle dotted

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.410
with the momentum
of the particle,

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.980
and then normalized
by the momentum.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:46.810
So basically, for a fermion,
which has a spin 1/2,

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:52.120
you get plus 1/2 if the
spin points in the momentum

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.850
direction and minus
1/2 if it points

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:57.020
in the opposite direction.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:01.630
So now, if you go back to our
particle here, off by here,

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:11.050
decaying into an electron and
a positron, spin is at 1/2,

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:15.140
but you find that an electron
is a left-handed particle,

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:18.730
so its helicity will
point in this direction.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:23.070
And for the positron--
sorry-- for the positron,

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.120
it points in the
same connection.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:31.000
So the pion here is
spin 0, and if you

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.280
discuss this in the
rest frame of the pion,

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.830
the electron and
the positron fly off

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:41.490
in opposite directions, which
means that the spin doesn't

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.600
in align to 0.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:47.110
So that's why this
is highly suppressed.

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:49.627
It's not 0, because
you can find--

00:04:49.627 --> 00:04:52.210
you can put [INAUDIBLE] into the
rest frame, where you're just

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:54.250
basically looking
at both particles

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:57.340
from one side that was coming
to you, and in that case,

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:58.000
it's allowed.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:02.850
But the spintronic configuration
is highly [INAUDIBLE]..

